  "system": {
    "finalName": "",
    "description": "<p><i>Reference Book: <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Star_Wars_Saga_Edition_Jedi_Academy_Training_Manual\" title=\"Star Wars Saga Edition Jedi Academy Training Manual\">Star Wars Saga Edition Jedi Academy Training Manual</a></i> </p><p>Mephite Crystals are considered the standard by which all <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Lightsaber\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Lightsaber\">Lightsaber</a> blades are judged. Almost all <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Lightsabers\" title=\"Lightsabers\">Lightsabers</a> wielded by Jedi Knights in the days of the Old Republic incorporate Mephite Adegan Crystals. Mephite Crystals are similar in structure to both <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Pontite_Crystal\" title=\"Pontite Crystal\">Pontite Crystals</a> and <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Ilum_Crystals\" title=\"Ilum Crystals\">Ilum Crystals</a>, even to the point where some xenogeologists have misidentified crystal grows on <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Ilum\" title=\"Ilum\">Ilum</a> as Mephite Crystals. A Mephite Crystal grants the standard +1 bonus on attack rolls to it's attuned wielder. </p>",
